===Etymology 2===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ser- (bind)}}
From {{inh|en|enm|sorten}}, from {{der|en|fro|sortir|t=to allot, sort}}, from {{der|en|la|sortīre|t=draw lots, divide, choose}}, from {{m|la|sors}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{senseid|en|separate according to certain criteria}} {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[separate]] items into different categories according to certain [[criterion|criteria]] that determine their sorts.
#: {{syn|en|categorize|class|classify|group}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Sort''' the letters in those bags into a separate pile for each language.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1704|author=Isaac Newton|title=Opticks|passage=And seeing the Rays which differ in Refrangibility may be parted and '''sorted''' from one another, and that either by Refraction..., or by Reflexion..., and then the several '''sorts''' apart at equal Incidences suffer unequal Refractions,...; it's manifest that the Sun's Light is an heterogeneous Mixture of Rays..., as was proposed.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1929|author=Percival Christopher Wren|title=Good Gestes, The McSnorrt Reminiscent|passage="Is there a man among ye has the Gaelic? ... Is there a man among ye can speak English even? ... Is there a man among ye at all? Ye gang o' lasceevious auld de'ils, decked oot like weemin, in spite o' yer hairy long whuskers, full beards and full skirts, ye deceitful besoms. Whuskers and petticoats wi' the vices o' both and the virtues o' neither. I'll sorrt ye." And there were sounds of alarums and excursions within.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en| date=August 27, 2017| author=Brandon Nowalk| title=Game Of Thrones slows down for the longest, and best, episode of the season (newbies)| work=The Onion AV Club| url=http://www.avclub.com/game-of-thrones-slows-for-the-longest-and-best-episod-1798483815| passage=Jaime finally leaves her [Cersei], walking right past his imminent executioner, and rides out of King’s Landing, finally neatly '''sorting''' our humans into good and evil and Bronn.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260905110726/https://www.avclub.com/game-of-thrones-slows-for-the-longest-and-best-episod-1798483815|archivedate=5 September 2026}}
# {{senseid|en|arrange into some sort of order}}{{lb|en|transitive}} To [[arrange]] into some sequence, usually [[numerically]], [[alphabetically]] or [[chronologically]].
#: {{syn|en|order|rank}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Sort''' those bells into a row in ascending sequence of pitch.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[conjoin]]; to put together in distribution; to [[class]].
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Francis Bacon|title=Sylva Sylvarum, Or, A Naturall Historie in Ten Centuries|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=x0akhiXCUnwC&pg=PP28|year=1635|passage=Shellfish have been, by some of the ancients, compared and '''sorted''' with ''insecta''.}}
